{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9cd2b52fc7d3cda0", "type": "tool_result", "content": "80463 /tmp/paper_2608_02138.txt\n The Role of Disfluencies in Speech Translation Report GitHub Issue × Title: Content selection saved. Describe the issue below: Description: Submit without GitHub Submit in GitHub arXiv is now an independent nonprofit! Learn more × Back to arXiv Why HTML? Report Issue Back to Abstract Download PDF Abstract 1 Introduction 2 The Role of Disfluencies 2.1 Methodology Data Selection: Switchboard. Human annotation of disfluency meaning. Analysis approach. 2.2 Analysis of Disfluency Annotations Removing disfluencies amplifies perceived negative emotion. Annotators diverge more when disfluencies are present. Can LLMs replace human annotators? Implications for translation. 3 Uh-Mazing Speech Translation 3.1 Human Translation Annotation Protocol. 3.2 Inter-annotator agreement on translation 3.3 The Role of Disfluencies in Different Languages Syntactic Context of Disfluencies. Context Shift on Translation. 4 Models & Evaluation 4.1 Translation Models 4.2 Evaluation Automatic Metrics. Disfluency Preservation. Human Evaluation of Quality. 5 Results 5.1 Comparison to Human Annotation and Automatic Metrics 5.2 Translation Quality Architecture. Prompt formulation. X → \\to EN Translation. 5.3 Disfluency Preservation Style vs. Meaning. 5.4 Effect of Disfluency Type Failure Mode Taxonomy. Quality by Disfluency Type. 6 Inference-Time Interventions Interventions. Inference-Time Interventions have impact on disfluent translation. 7 Discussion and Conclusion Disfluencies are meaningful, structured signals that are often not translated. Implications for practitioners and researchers. 8 Generative AI Use Disclosure 9 Acknowledgments References A Human Case Study of the Meaning Preservation of Disfluencies B Uh-Mazing Benchmark Details C Speech Translation Model Details D Results License: arXiv.org perpetual non-exclus